From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gyuyoung Kim <qkim@google.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:03:45 +0000
Subject: [M150-LTS][MediaSource] Match GOP keyframe PTS in FreeBuffers()

SourceBufferStream::Append() records the last-appended buffer timestamps
before merging adjacent later ranges into range_for_next_append_.
Because separate coded frame groups have independent timestamps, a
merged later GOP in range_for_next_append_ can share the same
back-buffer PTS and DTS as the last-appended GOP. Evicting that merged
GOP from the back caused FreeBuffers() to misidentify it as the
last-appended GOP, leaving append-sequence state out of sync with
range_for_next_append_ and allowing a subsequent split and non-keyframe
append to create a keyframe-less SourceBufferRange.

Track the keyframe PTS of the last-appended GOP and require it to match
the evicted GOP's leading keyframe PTS in FreeBuffers(), uniquely
identifying the GOP within range_for_next_append_. Also promote
SourceBufferRange leading-keyframe and non-empty keyframe_map_
invariants to CHECKs.

Fixed: 577402416
